text:
My true-love’s heart is mine, and mine is his—  
a trade of souls, a swap of stars in the dark.  
I clutch his soul like dawn, and he clings to mine;  
no pact was ever spun so sweet or so stark.  
His heart, within me, binds us as one thread;  
my heart, in him, steers his dreams through the night.  
He loves my heart, for once it was his own;  
I keep his because it’s bound to my light.  
His wound was carved by my gaze, my wound by his sting;  
the pain we trade, a dance of fire and frost.  
Equal scars, equal bliss, in this twist we cling—  
my true-love’s heart is mine, and mine is his.

